'''''Spiraea trilobata''''', known as '''Asian meadowsweet''', is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Rosaceae]].{{r|powo|usda}} It was [[species description|first formally named]] in 1771.{{r|ipni}} ''Spiraea trilobata'' is native to Asia.{{r|powo}} It has occasionally naturalized in the United States.{{r|usda}}

